karadoc <karadoc@gmail.com> wrote:
>> if each horn is tracked separately, what prevents a paranoid player from
>> simply keeping multiple horns?
>
> Nothing. In fact, it might be wise to keep multiple horns. I myself
> kept a spare horn in my bag even before this change. The main
> disadvantage to carrying multiple horns is just the extra weight. Do
> you think it's bad that extra horns can kind of get around this game
> mechanic?

No. It's also a gameplay decision. If you would really want that the
player only had one unicorn horn you would have to add code that
enforces it. I think it's nothing wrong in changing the unicorn horn's
behavior (even though players might not like it :-)

When changing the unicorn horn for a variant of NetHack, I think I've
seen these changes:
 - fix less troubles than in vanilla
 - make it have charges
 - make it less reliable
 - let it break after some usage
 - remove it entirely

Although I'm not sure about the last one.

